IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clwa-dates`
IMPORT `clwa-precourt`

-- Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002 (ACT), chapter 5 -- worked cases for the questions of the person bringing a personal
-- injury claim.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
-- Periods are counted as the Act gives them where no period is prescribed (the Regulation is not deposited), with the
-- month reading of fork F2 (corresponding day, or the month's last day).
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar date` d m y

`ANY DAY` MEANS `on` 1 1 2000

`ORDINARY` MEANS `a personal injury claim that is not a motor accident claim or a child abuse claim`
`MOTOR` MEANS `a motor accident claim`
`CHILD ABUSE` MEANS `a child abuse claim`

§ `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply`

-- A personal injury claim, no workers compensation: chapter 5 applies.
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: chapter 5 (the pre-court procedures) applies to your claim (s 50 (1))`
-- A motor accident common law claim, no workers compensation: chapter 5 applies (s 50 (1) names them).
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: chapter 5 (the pre-court procedures) applies to your claim (s 50 (1))`
-- The workers compensation claim itself.
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: chapter 5 does not apply to a claim for workers compensation itself (the text's no, s 50 (2) (a))`
-- Not a personal injury claim (a claim for property damage only).
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `chapter 5 is about claims for damages for personal injury; this is not one, and the Act says nothing more about it here (NOTHING-kind)`
-- Both Limitation Act s 30A notices given.
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: chapter 5 does not apply where both Limitation Act 1985 s 30A notices have been given (the text's no, s 50 (2) (b))`
-- Workers compensation claimed for the injury; the damages claim is only against the employer.
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a workers compensation claim was made for the injury (the text's no, s 50 (3))`
-- Workers compensation claimed, but the damages claim is a motor accident claim: part 5.2 only.
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only part 5.2 (claims procedures) applies: a workers compensation claim was made for the injury, but s 50 (4) keeps part 5.2; the rest of chapter 5 does not apply (the text's no, s 50 (3))`
-- Workers compensation claimed, and the damages claim is also against a negligent third party: part 5.2 only.
#ASSERT `s 50 -- does chapter 5 apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `only part 5.2 (claims procedures) applies: a workers compensation claim was made for the injury, but s 50 (4) keeps part 5.2; the rest of chapter 5 does not apply (the text's no, s 50 (3))`

§ `s 51 -- what time limit applies`

#ASSERT `s 51 -- what time limit applies to my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a fixed last day: the earlier of 9 months after the accident (or the first symptoms) and 4 months after you instructed a lawyer or identified the respondent, whichever is later (s 51 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 51 -- what time limit applies to my notice of claim` `MOTOR` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a fixed last day: 3 months after the latest of the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2019 days in s 51 (4)`
#ASSERT `s 51 -- what time limit applies to my notice of claim` `CHILD ABUSE` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no fixed day: a child abuse claim needs notice within a reasonable time before you begin the proceeding (s 51 (5))`
#ASSERT `s 51 -- what time limit applies to my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: you are under a legal disability, and need not give notice while it lasts; the period begins when it ends (s 60)`
-- The disability has ended: the ordinary limit applies, counted from its end.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- what time limit applies to my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a fixed last day: the earlier of 9 months after the accident (or the first symptoms) and 4 months after you instructed a lawyer or identified the respondent, whichever is later (s 51 (3))`

§ `s 51 -- the last day`

-- Accident 15 Jan 2026, symptoms at once, no lawyer yet, respondent identified that day: 9 months on, 15 Oct 2026.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 15 10 2026)
-- Same, lawyer first instructed 1 Mar 2026 (later than the respondent's identification): 4 months on, 1 Jul 2026, is earlier.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 1 7 2026)
-- Lawyer instructed 20 Jul 2026: limb (b) would be 20 Nov 2026, so limb (a), 15 Oct 2026, is earlier.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 20 7 2026) (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 15 10 2026)
-- Lawyer instructed 1 Mar 2026 but the respondent identified only 10 Jun 2026 (the later day): 10 Oct 2026, so 15 Oct 2026 is not earlier; 10 Oct 2026.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 10 6 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 10 10 2026)
-- Symptoms not immediately apparent; first appeared 31 May 2026: 9 months on is 28 Feb 2027 (no 31 February).
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) FALSE (`on` 31 5 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 28 2 2027)
-- Accident 31 Aug 2026; lawyer and respondent both 31 Oct 2026: limb (b) 4 months on is 28 Feb 2027, before limb (a) 31 May 2027.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 31 8 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 31 10 2026) (`on` 31 10 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 28 2 2027)
-- Accident 15 Dec 2026, across the year end: 15 Sep 2027.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 12 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 15 12 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 15 9 2027)
-- Motor accident claim, latest s 51 (4) day 10 Nov 2026: 3 months on, 10 Feb 2027.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `MOTOR` (`on` 1 3 2025) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 10 11 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 10 2 2027)
-- Motor, latest day 30 Nov 2026: 3 months on is 28 Feb 2027.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `MOTOR` (`on` 1 3 2025) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 30 11 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS JUST (`on` 28 2 2027)
-- Child abuse claim: no fixed day.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `CHILD ABUSE` (`on` 1 3 1990) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Still under a legal disability: no day yet.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` TRUE FALSE `ANY DAY` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A child injured 15 Jan 2026 turns 18 on 10 Jun 2030, no lawyer: 9 months after the disability ends, 10 Mar 2031.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` TRUE TRUE (`on` 10 6 2030) EQUALS JUST (`on` 10 3 2031)
-- The same child's parent instructed a lawyer on 1 Feb 2029: limb (b) is counted from 10 Jun 2030, so 10 Oct 2030 (fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 51 -- the last day for my notice of claim` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 1 2 2029) (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` TRUE TRUE (`on` 10 6 2030) EQUALS JUST (`on` 10 10 2030)

§ `s 51 -- have I given notice in time`

-- The facts of the 1 Jul 2026 case above, with what was done. Short form:
GIVEN `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice given on` IS A DATE, `excuse given` IS A BOOLEAN, `excuse given on` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My notice of claim`
`Ana's notice` `notice given` `notice given on` `excuse given` `excuse given on` `today` MEANS
    `s 51 -- have I given my notice of claim in time` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` `notice given` `notice given on` `excuse given` `excuse given on` `today`

-- Notice on the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `Ana's notice` TRUE (`on` 1 7 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `in time: you gave notice on or before the last day (s 51 (3) or (4))`
-- The day before: in time.
#ASSERT `Ana's notice` TRUE (`on` 30 6 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `in time: you gave notice on or before the last day (s 51 (3) or (4))`
-- The day after, no excuse: still owes the excuse.
#ASSERT `Ana's notice` TRUE (`on` 2 7 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `late, and you still owe a reasonable excuse for the delay, in the notice or by separate written notice (s 51 (7)); until it is given the notice is not given as required, and you cannot proceed unless the respondent or the court lets you (s 59)`
-- The day after, with the excuse in the notice.
#ASSERT `Ana's notice` TRUE (`on` 2 7 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 7 2026) (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `late, but you have given a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 51 (7)): the s 51 duty is met`
-- The day after, with the excuse by separate notice later.
#ASSERT `Ana's notice` TRUE (`on` 2 7 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 7 2026) (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `late, but you have given a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 51 (7)): the s 51 duty is met`
-- Not given; today the last day: still in time.
#ASSERT `Ana's notice` FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `not yet given, and the last day has not passed`
-- Not given; today the day after.
#ASSERT `Ana's notice` FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 2 7 2026) EQUALS `not yet given, and the last day has passed: you must still give it (the duty continues, Legislation Act 2001 s 152), with a reasonable excuse for the delay unless it is a motor accident claim (s 51 (7))`

-- Motor accident claim, last day 10 Feb 2027: on the day, in time; the day after, late with no excuse required (finding 4).
#ASSERT `s 51 -- have I given my notice of claim in time` `MOTOR` (`on` 1 3 2025) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 10 11 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 10 2 2027) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `in time: you gave notice on or before the last day (s 51 (3) or (4))`
#ASSERT `s 51 -- have I given my notice of claim in time` `MOTOR` (`on` 1 3 2025) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 10 11 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` TRUE (`on` 11 2 2027) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `late: s 51 (7) asks for an excuse only when the s 51 (3) period is missed, and says nothing for a motor accident claim (NOTHING-kind); the notice is not given within the s 51 (4) period`
-- Child abuse claim: no fixed last day.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- have I given my notice of claim in time` `CHILD ABUSE` (`on` 1 3 1990) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 3 2026) `ANY DAY` FALSE FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `no fixed last day: a child abuse claim needs notice within a reasonable time before you begin the proceeding (s 51 (5))`
-- Under a legal disability that has not ended.
#ASSERT `s 51 -- have I given my notice of claim in time` `ORDINARY` (`on` 15 1 2026) TRUE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 15 1 2026) `ANY DAY` TRUE FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `not yet required: you are under a legal disability, and the period begins when it ends (s 60)`

-- The regulative rule alone: in time on the last day; late with no excuse, not met; late with an excuse, met; for a
-- motor accident claim (no excuse required) a late notice discharges the continuing duty.
#ASSERT `the s 51 duties are met` (`on` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 7 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY`
#ASSERT (`the s 51 duties are met` (`on` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 7 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the s 51 duties are met` (`on` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 7 2026) TRUE (`on` 3 7 2026)
#ASSERT `the s 51 duties are met` (`on` 10 2 2027) FALSE (`on` 11 2 2027) FALSE `ANY DAY`

§ `s 54 -- is my notice taken to comply`

`DIRECT` MEANS `from the day it received my notice of claim (s 52 (1))`
`AFTER INFO` MEANS `from the day I gave it the further information it asked for (s 52 (2) (a), (3))`
`AFTER INSISTING` MEANS `from the day I told it I consider it properly a respondent (s 52 (2) (b) or (4) (b))`
`SATISFIED` MEANS `that it is satisfied my notice is a complying notice of claim`
`WAIVES` MEANS `that it is not satisfied, but waives the noncompliance`
`NOT SATISFIED` MEANS `that it is not satisfied and does not waive, allowing me a period to fix it`
`PRESUMED` MEANS `yes: the respondent gave no response within the required period, so it is conclusively presumed to be satisfied that your notice is a complying notice of claim (s 54 (3))`
`WAITING` MEANS `not yet decided: the respondent's required period has not ended and it has not responded`

-- Received 10 Mar 2026: the respondent's last day is 10 Apr 2026.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `DIRECT` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 4 2026) `SATISFIED` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `yes: the respondent's response says it is satisfied that your notice is a complying notice of claim (s 54 (2) (a))`
-- A response a day late, even one saying it is not satisfied: presumed satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `DIRECT` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 11 4 2026) `NOT SATISFIED` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `PRESUMED`
-- No response; today the last day: not yet.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `DIRECT` (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` `SATISFIED` (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `WAITING`
-- No response; today the day after: presumed.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `DIRECT` (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` `SATISFIED` (`on` 11 4 2026) EQUALS `PRESUMED`
-- In time, waives.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `DIRECT` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 4 2026) `WAIVES` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `the respondent waived the noncompliance (s 54 (2) (b)): you may proceed with the claim (s 59 (1) (b))`
-- In time, not satisfied and no waiver.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `DIRECT` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 4 2026) `NOT SATISFIED` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `not yet: the respondent is not satisfied and does not waive; it must allow you a reasonable period of at least 1 month to satisfy it or fix the noncompliance (s 54 (2) (c))`
-- Further information given 31 Jan 2026: the last day is 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `AFTER INFO` (`on` 31 1 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` `SATISFIED` (`on` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `WAITING`
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `AFTER INFO` (`on` 31 1 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` `SATISFIED` (`on` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `PRESUMED`
-- The claimant insisted on 15 May 2026; the respondent responded 15 Jun 2026, satisfied: in time.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is the respondent taken to be satisfied that my notice complies` `AFTER INSISTING` (`on` 15 5 2026) TRUE (`on` 15 6 2026) `SATISFIED` (`on` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `yes: the respondent's response says it is satisfied that your notice is a complying notice of claim (s 54 (2) (a))`

§ `s 54 (2) (c) -- the period to fix my notice`

#ASSERT `s 54 (2) (c) -- is the period to fix my notice long enough` (`on` 15 3 2026) (`on` 14 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS `too short: less than 1 month, which s 54 (2) (c) does not allow (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 54 (2) (c) -- is the period to fix my notice long enough` (`on` 15 3 2026) (`on` 15 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS `long enough: at least 1 month, and reasonable (s 54 (2) (c))`
#ASSERT `s 54 (2) (c) -- is the period to fix my notice long enough` (`on` 15 3 2026) (`on` 15 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS `at least 1 month, but not reasonable: not what s 54 (2) (c) requires (the text's no)`
-- From 31 Jan 2026 a month ends on 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `s 54 (2) (c) -- is the period to fix my notice long enough` (`on` 31 1 2026) (`on` 27 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS `too short: less than 1 month, which s 54 (2) (c) does not allow (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 54 (2) (c) -- is the period to fix my notice long enough` (`on` 31 1 2026) (`on` 28 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS `long enough: at least 1 month, and reasonable (s 54 (2) (c))`

§ `s 59, s 62, s 79 -- going further`

#ASSERT `s 59 -- can I proceed further with my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you gave a complying notice of claim`
#ASSERT `s 59 -- can I proceed further with my claim` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent has said in writing that it is satisfied, or that you have remedied the noncompliance (s 59 (1) (a) (i))`
#ASSERT `s 59 -- can I proceed further with my claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent is presumed to be satisfied that your notice complies (s 59 (1) (a) (ii), s 54 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 59 -- can I proceed further with my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent waived the noncompliance (s 59 (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 59 -- can I proceed further with my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court declared the noncompliance remedied, or authorised you to proceed (s 59 (1) (c)), on any conditions it set (s 59 (2))`
#ASSERT `s 59 -- can I proceed further with my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: without a complying notice, and none of the s 59 (1) exceptions, you cannot proceed further with the claim (the text's no)`

#ASSERT `s 62 -- can I get interest for a period I was not complying` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you were complying with part 5.2 in that period: s 62 (1) (b) does not limit interest for it`
#ASSERT `s 62 -- can I get interest for a period I was not complying` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `interest may be awarded for that period: the court is satisfied you had a reasonable excuse (s 62 (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 62 -- can I get interest for a period I was not complying` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no interest for that period: the court may award it only if satisfied you had a reasonable excuse, and it is not (the text's no, s 62 (1) (b))`

#ASSERT `s 79 -- can I begin a proceeding now` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not under s 79: the court has not given leave for an urgent need; you must first comply with chapter 5 (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 79 -- can I begin a proceeding now` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave for an urgent need; the proceeding is stayed until you comply with chapter 5 (or it ends) (s 79 (1), (3))`
#ASSERT `s 79 -- can I begin a proceeding now` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave, and it is not stayed: you have a terminal condition, the trial is to be expedited and given priority; chapter 5 (other than s 79) no longer applies to the injury (s 79 (4), (5))`
-- Terminal condition, but no priority order: still stayed (both s 79 (4) (a) and (b) are needed).
#ASSERT `s 79 -- can I begin a proceeding now` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave for an urgent need; the proceeding is stayed until you comply with chapter 5 (or it ends) (s 79 (1), (3))`

§ `s 61 -- the attempt to resolve the claim`

`NO OFFER YET` MEANS `the respondent has not made an offer yet, and its 6 months have not ended (s 61 (1))`
`RESPONDENT LATE` MEANS `the respondent did not make a written offer or settle within 6 months (s 61 (1)): a court may award you costs caused by it (s 62 (2)) and may order it to comply (s 78)`
`MY TIME RUNNING` MEANS `the respondent made an offer, and your 3 months to answer it in writing have not ended (s 61 (4))`
`BOTH MET` MEANS `the respondent made an offer, and you answered it in writing within 3 months (s 61 (4)): both duties are met`
`I AM LATE` MEANS `the respondent made an offer, and you did not answer it in writing within 3 months (s 61 (4)): a court may award the respondent costs caused by it (s 62 (1))`

-- Complying notice received 10 Mar 2026: the respondent's last day is 10 Sep 2026.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 10 9 2026) EQUALS `NO OFFER YET`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 11 9 2026) EQUALS `RESPONDENT LATE`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 11 9 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `RESPONDENT LATE`
-- Offer on the respondent's last day, 10 Sep 2026: the claimant's last day is 10 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 9 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 12 2026) (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `BOTH MET`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 9 2026) TRUE (`on` 11 12 2026) (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `I AM LATE`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 9 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 10 12 2026) EQUALS `MY TIME RUNNING`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 9 2026) FALSE `ANY DAY` (`on` 11 12 2026) EQUALS `I AM LATE`
-- Offer received 31 Aug 2026: 3 months on is 30 Nov 2026.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 31 8 2026) TRUE (`on` 30 11 2026) (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `BOTH MET`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- where does the attempt to resolve my claim stand` (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 31 8 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 12 2026) (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `I AM LATE`

§ `Deadlines -- the respondent's steps`

#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `tell me about anyone else who may be liable, and send them my notice (s 51 (9)): counted from the day it received my notice` (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 10 4 2026
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `tell me about anyone else who may be liable, and send them my notice, for a motor accident claim (s 51A): counted from the day it received my notice` (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 17 3 2026
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `give me its preliminary response (s 52 (1)): counted from the day it received my notice` (`on` 31 1 2026) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `respond after I gave it the further information it asked for (s 52 (3)): counted from the day I gave the information` (`on` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 30 4 2026
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `tell me whether it is satisfied with my fix (s 54 (4)): counted from the day the period it gave me ends` (`on` 15 4 2026) EQUALS `on` 15 5 2026
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `say whether it admits liability and make an offer or settle (s 61 (1)): counted from the day it received my complying notice` (`on` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `respond in writing to my settlement offer (s 61 (4)): counted from the day it received the offer` (`on` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `on` 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `give me copies of its reports and documents about the accident and my condition (s 68 (2) (a)): counted from the day it received my complying notice` (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 10 4 2026
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `give me a report or document that came into its possession later (s 68 (2) (b)): counted from the day it came into its possession` (`on` 28 12 2026) EQUALS `on` 4 1 2027
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `answer my request for information about the accident (s 68 (3)): counted from the day it received the request` (`on` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `on` 15 1 2027
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must the respondent take this step` `give me copies I required, out of material it offered for inspection (s 71 (4)): counted from the day I made the requirement or, over 200 pages, the day I paid` (`on` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 30 4 2026

§ `Deadlines -- my steps`

#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must I take this step` `give the respondent the further information it asked for, or insist it is properly a respondent (s 52 (2)): counted from the day it told me` (`on` 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (`on` 15 2 2026)
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must I take this step` `accept, or dispute, the respondent's statement that it is not properly a respondent (s 52 (4)): counted from the day it told me` (`on` 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (`on` 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must I take this step` `give the respondent copies of my reports and documents about the accident and my condition (s 64 (2) (a)): counted from the day I gave notice of the claim` (`on` 31 10 2026) EQUALS JUST (`on` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must I take this step` `give the respondent a report or document that came into my possession later (s 64 (2) (b)): counted from the day it came into my possession` (`on` 26 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (`on` 5 3 2026)
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must I take this step` `answer the respondent's reasonable request for information (s 64 (3)): counted from the day I received the request` (`on` 1 2 2028) EQUALS JUST (`on` 1 3 2028)
-- 30 Nov 2027 + 3 months: 29 Feb 2028 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must I take this step` `respond in writing to the respondent's settlement offer (s 61 (4)): counted from the day I received the offer` (`on` 30 11 2027) EQUALS JUST (`on` 29 2 2028)
#ASSERT `chapter 5 -- by when must I take this step` `tell each other respondent that I added a later respondent (s 55 (3) (b)): only a period prescribed by regulation` (`on` 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 66, 67, 71`

#ASSERT `s 66 -- must the respondent reimburse me for the expert report` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the respondent must reimburse you the reasonable cost of the report (s 66 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 66 -- must the respondent reimburse me for the expert report` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: you must ask the respondent to reimburse you (s 66 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 66 -- must the respondent reimburse me for the expert report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `as your agreement with the respondent says: s 66 (1) is subject to it (s 66 (2))`
#ASSERT `s 66 -- must the respondent reimburse me for the expert report` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 66 applies only to a report obtained by agreement whose cost you are liable for (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 66 -- must the respondent reimburse me for the expert report` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 66 applies only to a report obtained by agreement whose cost you are liable for (the text's no)`

`MUST ATTEND` MEANS `yes: you must undergo the examination or assessment, at the respondent's expense, by the doctor or expert you select from its panel (s 67 (2))`
`PANEL TOO SMALL` MEANS `no: the panel is too small: at least 3 doctors or experts, or 2 if 3 with the right qualifications are not available (the text's no, s 67 (2), (4))`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- must I undergo the respondent's examination` TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `MUST ATTEND`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- must I undergo the respondent's examination` TRUE TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `PANEL TOO SMALL`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- must I undergo the respondent's examination` TRUE TRUE 2 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MUST ATTEND`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- must I undergo the respondent's examination` TRUE TRUE 1 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `PANEL TOO SMALL`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- must I undergo the respondent's examination` TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: you are not obliged, because it is unreasonable or unnecessarily repetitious (s 67 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- must I undergo the respondent's examination` FALSE TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 67 applies only where the respondent failed to get your agreement to a joint report, and asks for the examination at its own expense (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 67 -- must I undergo the respondent's examination` TRUE FALSE 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 67 applies only where the respondent failed to get your agreement to a joint report, and asks for the examination at its own expense (the text's no)`

